          ],
          "content": "(b) One-hundredth or 90 thousandths?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.112,
            0.606,
            0.131
          ],
          "content": "(c) One-thousandth or 90 hundredths?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.135,
            0.847,
            0.174
          ],
          "content": "14. Write the decimal forms of the quantities mentioned (an example is given):"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.178,
            0.69,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "(a) 87 ones, 5 tenths and 60 hundredths = 88.10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.203,
            0.47,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": "(b) 12 tens and 12 tenths"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.226,
            0.713,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "(c) 10 tens, 10 ones, 10 tenths, and 10 hundredths"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.25,
            0.713,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "(d) 25 tens, 25 ones, 25 tenths, and 25 hundredths"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.274,
            0.82,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": "15. Using each digit 0 – 9 not more than once, fill the boxes below so that the sum is closest to 10.5:"
