            0.152,
            0.454,
            0.648,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "16. Write the following fractions in decimal form:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.481,
            0.281,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": "(a) $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.529,
            0.28,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": "(c) $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.486,
            0.48,
            0.551,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": "(b) $\\frac { 3 } { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.486,
            0.529,
            0.551,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": "(d) $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.576,
            0.28,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "(e) $\\frac{1}{5}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.486,
            0.577,
            0.55,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "(f) 4 $\\frac{4}{5}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.644,
            0.591,
            0.667
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.675,
            0.832,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "We can split a unit into smaller parts to get more exact/accurate measurements."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.713,
            0.71,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "• We extended the Indian place value system and saw that"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.733,
            0.428,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "» 1 unit = 10 one-tenths,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.752,
            0.487,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": "» 1 tenth = 10 one-hundredths,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.771,
            0.542,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": "» 1 hundredth = 10 one-thousandths,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.791,
            0.488,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "» 10 one-hundredths = 1 tenth,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.81,
            0.487,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": "» 100 one-hundredths = 1 unit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.828,
            0.831,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": "A decimal point (‘.’) is used in the Indian place value system to separate the whole number part of a number from its fractional part."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.867,
            0.832,
            0.905
          ],
          "content": "We also learnt how to compare decimal numbers, locate them on the number line, and perform addition and subtraction on them."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.939,
            0.186,
            0.954
          ],
          "content": "80"
        },
